            <ArticleTitle>Photodynamic Therapy With Topical 5% 5-Aminolevulinic Acid for the Treatment of Truncal Acne in Asian Patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>727-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Photodynamic therapy (PDT) using topical application of aminolevulinic acid (ALA) is an effective treatment for acne vulgaris. However, there is no clear consensus on the treatment regime in Asians.&lt;BR /&gt;</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the efficacy, safety and tolerability of 5% ALA PDT in the treatment of truncal acne in Asians.&lt;BR /&gt;</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Patients with truncal acne were treated with 5%-ALA under occlusion for 3 hours. All were subsequently treated with a red light source at wavelength 630 nm and an irradiance of 38mW/cm&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; giving a total dose of 37 J/cm&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;. The numbers of acne lesions were recorded at baseline and regular intervals after treatment together with any adverse effects.&lt;BR /&gt;</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Fifteen patients were recruited. Overall, there was a 64.2% reduction in the inflammatory lesions count and a 24.3% reduction in the non-inflammatory lesions count at the end of the 12 weeks follow-up. Both mean lesions counts were significantly lower than baseline at all follow-up time points with paired t tests (all P values &amp;lt;0.05). Pain was well tolerated among our patients.&lt;BR /&gt;</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">A single treatment session of 5%-ALA PDT was effective for the treatment of truncal acne with little side effects and acceptable in our Asian patients.&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt; &lt;em&gt;J Drugs Dermatol&lt;/em&gt;. 2016;15(6):727-732.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
